The test vehicle travels at target speed V1 on a straight road. Pedestrians waiting to cross the current lane are positioned on the left/right side of the current lane, with a distance D between them and the lane centerline. When the longitudinal separation distance between the test vehicle and the pedestrian is d, the pedestrian crosses the current lane from the left/right side of the test vehicle at speed V2. The time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is equal to the time required for the pedestrian to reach the collision point.